{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791429952,"nonce":"izBP2Ja4iKFZ6dS2IFBqWafBraA=","message":"Landed in commit 47518ab2472f7c700c507e518c49aefde1a8de5f. Shared HIR now carries consecutive integer vector counters, normalizes representable constant inclusive bounds, interleaves small reductions across four independent accumulators, preserves scalar tails and live-outs, and rejects unsafe shapes. LLVM-enabled pipelines retain scalar reductions for LLVM to select its native vector width. Interpreter-first dispatch and all existing native probes remain enabled.\n\nValidated on macOS: 419 compiler unit tests, 4 counter-vector tests across interpreter/Cranelift/LLVM, 14 OSR-transfer tests, 6 LLVM-helper tests, and the promoted-stub test pass. The 4 new counter tests also pass without LLVM support compiled in. NUC native tests and conformance pass with LLVM off and on (43 Lua and 50 Python categories; three official Lua suites excluded).\n\nFive alternating NUC rounds, LLVM OFF, affinity 0-7: free_function_call at 100 million iterations goes from 53.985 to 28.187 ms kernel and 74.141 to 49.422 ms wall; the same candidate with counter vectorization disabled is 54.345/74.525 ms. At one billion iterations: 533.993 to 259.886 ms kernel, 554.391 to 280.878 ms wall. LuaJIT is 49.117 ms wall at normal size and 471.065 ms long. LLVM reference is still faster, 35.406 ms normal and 73.273 ms long; candidate LLVM retains those numbers at 35.926 and 73.151 ms. Tiny-run startup remains about 20 ms versus LuaJIT about 2 ms. No claim of beating LLVM or all kernels.\n\nThe broader probe-removal experiment was withheld under its separate issue because LU regressed. The accepted candidate restores LU: 673.460 ms baseline wall versus 672.028 ms candidate in the full sweep. Do not attribute the held roughly 33 ms call-loop result to this commit. Artifacts on NUC: /tmp/zyntax-counter-accepted-lengths.json, /tmp/zyntax-counter-accepted-native-tests.log, /tmp/zyntax-counter-accepted-conformance-{off,on}.log, /tmp/zyntax-nuc-counter-accepted-all-*.json. Full sweep still completing; final checksum summary to follow.","files":null}]}